<title>FRANCE: Rhone-Poulenc 1996 profit up 28.4 pct.</title>
<headline>Rhone-Poulenc 1996 profit up 28.4 pct.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996.</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of French francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net income				   2,740  vs	   2,134</p>
<p>    Net earnings per share (francs)	 8.44  vs	   6.71</p>
<p>    Gross dividend (francs)		   5.25  vs   up 16.7 pct</p>
<p>    Operating				    6,892  vs	   6,223</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit			     6,186  vs	   4,958</p>
<p>    Net interest expense		     2,151  vs	   1,726</p>
<p>    Turnover				    85,818  vs	  84,793</p>
<p>NOTE - Rhone-Poulenc gave the figures in a statement. It said earnings per share rose by 25.8 percent despite the negative impact of minus 0.64 francs per share linked to the recall and halt of production of certain Centeon products.</p>
<p>It linked net income rise mostly to earnings growth in the pharmaceuticals and animal and plant health businesses.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
